On Tue, 4 Jan 2005, Klaus Kassner wrote:
> Philipp Lucas schrieb:
 [how to spend an early wish on poison resistance]
> > +3 Green DSM: Get the AC bonus and poison resistance. Later, you can get
> > MR from a cloak and reflection from a shield or an amulet, so Grey or
> > Silver DSM are not necessary.
>
> I don't think that this is a viable option.  If you have seven wishes, you
> should get at least MR immediately.  Otherwise, a wand of death or a polymorph
> trap might end your game that started so micely (the latter might not be so
> bad, because you would become a green dragon).

Polymorph traps are no problem, for the reason you stated; they will rip
your cloak, if it is not a cloak of MR, but in this case it is not really
important in the long run, as you will have a CoMR later on anyway. And
how common are wands of death relatively to poison traps and poisoned
orcish arrows? When I am not already poison resistant, I spend a single
early wish on Green DSM.

With seven wishes, I would still take the Green DSM, and add a CoMR and an
amulet of reflection.

> Also being able to have
> reflection only by the amulet would not be desirable towards later stages of
> the game,

I often wear an amulet of reflection in Gehennom and on the ascension.

> Moreover, since a corpse of a green dragon can give you poison resistance with
> certainty, you don't need the scale mail at all.  Just wish for the corpse or
> rather for a tin of it, if that works.

It works, and you will get the poison resistance, but you give up on the
early AC bonus (if it is a single wish).

